      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to  $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y)?$",
      "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x$ is \n        \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the second definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y) & =\\frac{{e}^{2(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y)}-1}{{e}^{2(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y)}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y}-1}{{e}^{6\\operatorname{ln}\u2061y}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{y}^{6}}-1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{y}^{6}}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{6}-1}{{y}^{6}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
